    "messages": [
      {
        "id": "1562225186294468672",
        "sender": "jukalang",
        "text": "@everyone Looking for beta testers to test the new JukaHub features.",
        "timestamp": "2026-10-20T22:05:09.153Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "1562526758278926367",
        "sender": "lohesu",
        "text": "thats awesome",
        "timestamp": "2026-10-21T18:03:29.517Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "1562550647528759397",
        "sender": "jukalang",
        "text": "if you have any suggestions on what to add next, let me know. My progress is a little bet slower compared to the \"new Apps that are developed\" as I tend to manually test and rewrite things. I try to add more safety checks and maintain applications long term.",
        "timestamp": "2026-10-21T19:38:25.158Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "1562606820277887048",
        "sender": "jukalang",
        "text": "I've tried Claude AI code to improve my code and it just made a mess...Claude may be good for simple project but for complex dealing with system files, it just glitches. I think I will rely on my own edits going forward with JukaHub (especially when it comes to system files).",
        "timestamp": "2026-10-21T23:21:37.785Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "1562607184830005320",
        "sender": "jukalang",
        "text": "My UI might not be the best looking or get the best features, but I will try to focus more on security, reliability, and long term support",
        "timestamp": "2026-10-21T23:23:04.701Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "1562636605045346305",
        "sender": "You",
        "text": "j",
        "timestamp": "2026-10-22T01:19:59.027Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "1562636681679732747",
        "sender": "jukalang",
        "text": "Hi",
        "timestamp": "2026-10-22T01:20:17.298Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "1562636703267819593",
        "sender": "jukalang",
        "text": "How are you?",
        "timestamp": "2026-10-22T01:20:22.445Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "1562817315202932797",
        "sender": "davidemaglio",
        "text": "hi. if i want to install it into NextUI (i have a Trimui Brick) I need to add .pak to folder and put into Tools? i created Apps folder but it's missing into NextUI",
        "timestamp": "2026-10-22T13:18:03.686Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "1562851299572318330",
        "sender": "jukalang",
        "text": "\u003c@703521917419651142\u003e If I remember correctly, did you dump the actual contents of the folder into .pak folder or did you keep JukaHub-Trimui as a subdirectory? I believe you have to dump the actual files into JukaHub-Trimui.pak and it will show up.",
        "timestamp": "2026-10-22T15:33:06.191Z"
      }
